Subject: Re: Build up a finite queue without rejecting arrivals
Message-ID: <_eLoVGIi5tg.S9dnJt3RBAAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <_eLoVGIi5tg.FpPpmKbQAAAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
References: <_eLoVGIi5tg.m2GjogkxDAAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com> <_eLoVGIi5tg.FpPpmKbQAAAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/simmer-devel/c/_eLoVGIi5tg/m/S9dnJt3RBAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If you are wondering what solution I ended up using, here it is:

Within the seize/release block of the first resource, after the resource's timeout I branched off to check the queue length of the next resource in the line, if the queue was maxed out I used a trap/wait/untrap within that branch to wait for a signal that the queue had space available.  The signal was sent after the next resource was released if the current queue count of the resource was less than the total queue size of said resource.

I did this in succession down the line for each resource and it seems to be working, my last step is to factor in and test conveyor belt times between resources.

Here's the partial code below:

  # RESOURCE1 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        seize('resource1') %>%
          timeout(abs(rnorm(1,run_times['resource1'],.005))) %>%
          branch( function() (get_queue_count(fill_line, 'resource2') == get_queue_size(fill_line, 'resource2'))

                , continue = T
                , trajectory() %>%

                    trap('resource2_queue_open') %>%
                    wait () %>%
                    untrap('resource2_queue_open')) %>%
        release('resource1') %>%
  # RESOURCE2 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        seize('resource2') %>%
          timeout(abs(rnorm(1,run_times['resource2'],.005))) %>%
          branch( function() (get_queue_count(fill_line, 'resource3') == get_queue_size(fill_line, 'resource3'))

                , continue = T
                , trajectory() %>%

                    trap('resource3_queue_open') %>%
                    wait () %>%
                    untrap('resource3_queue_open')) %>%
        release('resource2') %>%
        branch( function() (get_queue_count(fill_line, 'resource2') < get_queue_size(fill_line, 'resource2'))

              , continue = T
              , trajectory() %>%

                send('resource2_queue_open')) %>%
  # RESOURCE3 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
...etc...

Thanks for your suggestions.

Best,
John

