> I've got the following trajectory for a patient who can be admitted or sent
> for tests or discharged. what i need is the patients going for tests to come
> back and go to either admitted or discharged

This trajectory allows a patient to be sent for tests more than once,
because you are exposing them to the branch decision more than once.
Is that what you want?

> However, when i run it with
>
> env2 <- simmer("patientpathway")%>%
>   add_resource("admit",2)%>%
>   add_resource("tests",3)%>%
>   add_resource("discharge",3)%>%
>   add_generator("patient", patient,function(){rpois(1,5)},mon=2)%>%
>   run(1000)
>
> arrivals <- get_mon_arrivals(env2,per_resource=TRUE)
>
> and look at the arrivals, some of the patients are going for tests and then
> disappearing, which isn't what I want and I can't figure out where I'm going
> wrong.

Note that times=1. Therefore, those patients who are entering the
tests trajectory for a second time don't rollback. These are your
"disappearing" arrivals.

> weirdly, some patients are (correctly) getting tests, then getting admitted
> or getting discharged.

These are those patients who are, by chance, entering the tests
trajectory just once.

